<rml>
<head>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="theme.rcss"/>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="sidebar_hud.rcss"/>
</head>
<body data-model="sidebar_hud">
    <!-- Tier 7 sidebar HUD (game::draw_panels). A PERSISTENT, render-only,
         continuous every-turn document — NOT a modal open/loop/close screen. It is
         opened once during gameplay and synced each turn; modal screens stack above
         it by open order. The body is transparent so the cleared (black) sidebar
         region shows through; only migrated panels paint.

         Slice 2b owns Sound / Stats / Needs. The owned panels are NOT contiguous in
         the layout (Mana can sit between Stats and Needs), so each fragment is its
         OWN absolutely-positioned element — game::draw_panels reports each panel's
         cell rect and sidebar_hud_position() places the matching element by id. Each
         fragment's text is built by its hud_*_text() producer + cata_text_to_rml()
         and bound to its model var. Further panels add their own element + var. -->
    <div id="hud-col" class="hud-col">
        <div id="hud-Sound" class="hud-panel" data-rml="sound_rml"></div>
        <div id="hud-Stats" class="hud-panel" data-rml="stats_rml"></div>
        <div id="hud-Needs" class="hud-panel" data-rml="needs_rml"></div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
